Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operator: 'crack tn36 L4's scale-collision interaction and solve it.' DONE.

TWO things cracked:
1. THE MECHANIC: L4 needs a scale-down interleaved with the moves. The object's
   bounding box CHANGES SIZE when scaled (adjust_scale, tn36.py:2283), and
   cwtesiybfx reverts collisions -> the straight order [3,3,3,3,1,9] LOSES, but
   interleaving the scale at the right point wins (e.g. [3,9,3,1,3,3]). The
   ordering search finds it (8 of 30 orderings win).
2. THE SOLVER BUG that masked it: iterating many orderings on ONE reused env trips
   the game's LOSS condition after ~12 failed runs and RESETS the whole episode to
   L0 (18/30 attempts were silently operating on L0). Fix: a FRESH env per ordering
   attempt, replayed through the known wins to the current level.

Now reproduces L1-L4 (reproduced=True claimed_level=4, 37 clicks). Registry: tn36
levels_reproduced 3->4, reproducible_total 18->19.

L5 frontier: needs a PROPERTY change (sjmtdfxdrc 11->15, codes 14/15/63 =
knfgrcbayu, not yet decoded). Logged with a concrete decode plan.
